{"full":"hf:Mihir1107/TheSnitch","spaceId":"Mihir1107/TheSnitch","name":"The Snitch","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":5,"created":"2026-04-21T08:03:41.000Z","updated":"2026-04-26T10:27:38.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://mihir1107-thesnitch.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Mihir1107/TheSnitch","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:35.731Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:35.731Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:35.731Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🕵️","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An OpenEnv environment for training and measuring AI systems that audit other AI systems.","Who watches the watchers? The Snitch is an OpenEnv environment for measuring AI oversight: an overseer reads another agent's tool-use trace and classifies its behavior as honest, reward-hacking, lazy, or deceptive — and must cite the specific trace step that gave the misbehavior away.","Headline finding: across four frontier instruction-tuned models — GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct — zero of 275 correctly-classified misbehavior traces both cited the correct trace step AND echoed the smoking-gun keyword. A 1.5B LoRA trained on the grounded reward captured both on 34 of 61. Frontier models classify misbehavior at the trace level but struggle to localize it. See BLOG.md for the full writeup."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Mihir1107/TheSnitch/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"946ebc0d5ca782cde67c9bb5a734521a7ab24d2230d99fc0e7bea8fa0bf1db99","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:35.788Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:35.788Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An OpenEnv environment for training and measuring AI systems that audit other AI syst